# Byte-identical checkouts on every machine and every platform. The repo stores LF and
# every checkout keeps LF, whatever core.autocrlf that machine happens to have (it is
# `true` on the Windows boxes here, which would otherwise rewrite the tree to CRLF while
# a Linux agent session sees LF — one commit, two different sets of bytes). This keeps the
# embedded assets, and therefore the emitted codebase-dsm.html, byte-stable regardless of
# where the tool is built.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch stays CRLF on every platform, including Linux. cmd.exe is DOCUMENTED to mis-parse
# LF-only .bat (labels, `call :label`, multi-line `( ... )` blocks), but that was measured
# TOLERANT on Windows 11 26200 across all of those constructs on 2026-08-24 — so this pin
# is the declared guarantee, not an observed necessity, and it holds because tolerance is
# a property of the build and nothing should rest on which build runs the file.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
